\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Chief Balken highlighted the work of the department\rquote s K\u8209?9 Unit, which consists of seven teams handling building searches, apprehensions, drug detection, and recovery of weapons and evidence. He shared operational statistics from the past year, including nearly 700 drug sniffs, 849 arrests (138 attributable directly to K\u8209?9 operations), multiple bite captures, and the seizure of firearms, narcotics, and illicit cash. The unit logged more than 1,800 hours of training. Chief Balken concluded by noting that he will soon request acquisition of an explosives\u8209?detection K\u8209?9, funded entirely through community donations, due to recent incidents requiring outside agency assistance.\par
\par
}

