\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 City Engineer Sean Lanier provided an overview of the City\rquote s MS4 stormwater conveyance system and its required permit, explaining that although the system is closed, stormwater ultimately discharges into Florida\rquote s right\u8209?of\u8209?way and flows toward Half Mile Creek. He outlined the City\rquote s five focus areas for controlling pollution-sanitation, stormwater maintenance, fleet, water resources, and code enforcement-and noted 116 stormwater\u8209?related citizen service requests in 2025. He described ongoing operations including maintenance of public and private retention areas, erosion control, debris removal, and staff certifications. Lanier also reported on sanitation initiatives such as Amnesty Day tire collection and electronic and household hazardous waste programs, as well as fleet recycling of batteries, oil, and filters. He emphasized code enforcement\rquote s role in preventing illicit discharges, gave examples of common pollutants, and highlighted the importance of proper disposal practices, yard waste management, and pet waste cleanup to reduce contaminants and nitrates. He concluded by reminding residents that everyday activities on land directly affect local water quality.\par
\par
