\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Council Member Hilty criticized the lack of public disclosure regarding a recent fraud case involving nearly $500,000 and urged greater transparency. Mr. Lee responded that the investigation is still ongoing, the internal auditor and IT staff are reviewing the matter, partial recovery and insurance claims are underway, and he denied any intent to conceal information. The discussion broadened to concerns about staff interactions with citizens and code enforcement practices, with Mr. Lee emphasizing that most staff\u8209?public interactions are positive and that unresolved issues often stem from missing plans or nonattendance at hearings. He agreed to provide a full report once the Internal Auditor's report is complete.\par
\par
Council Pro Tem Musleh commented he believes it would have been prudent to wait until the internal auditor's review was available and have a plan as to any corrective action to be taken. He stated he is all for full transparency, but it wouldn't have taken anything away from the public if it hadn't been disclosed until the next Council meeting when the report was complete.\par
