{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Police Chief Balken reported that the department handled 7,700 incidents during the period, a 1% decrease from last year. Dispatch calls increased by 7%, while self\u8209?initiated activity decreased by 4%. Traffic stops rose slightly, and traffic crashes declined by 1%. Crime saw modest increases across violent, property, and societal categories. He highlighted several recent cases, including the safe resolution of a dangerous family dispute, the arrest of an individual attempting to solicit a minor, and the conclusion of multiple long\u8209?term investigations resulting in significant sentences for theft, sex offender violations, and major drug trafficking. He noted that the department remains actively engaged in protecting vulnerable residents and addressing serious criminal activity.\par
\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Fire Chief Welborn reported 1,090 calls during the two\u8209?week period, bringing the annual total to 16,339. Engine 4 responded to 104 incidents and Engine 1 to 100 incidents. The department handled 76 motor vehicle accidents, seven fires, and 47 community calls. He highlighted a grease fire contained to a commercial kitchen, noting it was one of four such kitchen fires in the period, as well as two vehicle fires - one resulting from a crash and one from a mechanical malfunction.\par
\par
}

