{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 City Manager Peter Lee explained that staff collaborated to address the issue and that most of the insurance reimbursement had been recovered, leaving a loss of about $27-28,000. He noted that two employees are no longer with the city as a result. Chief of Staff Chris Watt added that the incident occurred because established procedures were not followed, and updated safeguards are now in place. Mayor Marciano confirmed that these procedures are expected to protect the city moving forward, and Mr. Lee emphasized the importance of maintaining strong insurance coverage despite the cost to taxpayers.\par
\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Mr. Panzagraft expressed frustration that, after repeatedly calling and leaving messages seeking general information about a the fraud incident, he was hung up on, ignored, and unable to reach city leadership. He said this felt like a violation of his right to ask questions of his government. Mayor Marciano responded that he was unaware of his messages until that afternoon; Mr. Lee had no messages left on his office phone. Council President Bethea explained that an active investigation limited what could be discussed. He further acknowledged his concerns but stated they could not answer questions they did not have information for and moved the meeting forward.\par
\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Ms. Fulton explained that her business is an alcohol\u8209?free, state\u8209?regulated food establishment and asked to be included in future discussions about kratom. She emphasized that her business does not sell synthetic products, supports stronger standards and testing for kratom, and proposed serving as a regulated dispensary for the natural leaf. She highlighted her eight years in business, commitment to safety and integrity, and willingness to collaborate. \par
\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Ms. Thomas explained that she has lived in her inherited family home for five years without heat or hot water and recently learned her pipes had been tampered with. She said she was removed from the city\rquote s housing rehabilitation list without notice due to a decades\u8209?old lien and only reinstated after inquiring. She asked for clear guidance on when her home will be scheduled for repairs, noting the hardships she has faced, and staff assured her they would move her request forward as quickly as possible.\par
\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Councilman Hilty asked staff whether records existed to confirm Mr. Panzagraft\rquote s repeated calls and messages. Mr. Watt responded that Mr. Panzagraft\rquote s account was inaccurate, explaining that they had spoken with him previously, that his calls were often irate, and that hang\u8209?ups occurred only after he refused to accept that the investigation report was not yet ready. Mr. Watt said all switchboard calls are recorded, that he attempted to update Mr. Panzagraft once the report was complete, and that he ultimately provided it to him in person.\par
\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
