\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Mr. Panzagraft said he values leadership and transparency and described difficulty reaching the city manager regarding questions about recent financial issues and FDOT\rquote s camera directive. He praised the police chief and Clerk\rquote s Office for being responsive and transparent but said he felt disrespected and delayed-nearly a month-when trying to speak with the city manager and city attorney. He also felt a prior meeting interaction, where the Chief of Staff told him to sit down, was unprofessional. He asked the Council to look into what he sees as a lack of transparency and timely communication.\par
\par
Council President Bethea thanked him, said no one was trying to dismiss him, and explained that some information couldn\rquote t be shared earlier because the investigation was still ongoing. Mr. Bethea emphasized that staff had tried to communicate but noted that when conversations become heated, it\rquote s harder for staff to respond productively. He affirmed that the concerns were taken seriously and thanked Mr. Panzagraft for addressing them respectfully.\par
\par
}

