{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Council Member Dreyer raised concerns about a local business being charged high county transportation impact fees and asked for a status update on the city\rquote s long\u8209?discussed shift toward a mobility\u8209?fee system. Growth Management Director Jeff Shrum explained that the City has drafted proposed changes to the interlocal agreement with the County, including language for proportionate\u8209?share projects, and is working to schedule another meeting to resolve remaining issues. City Manager Pete Lee added that major topics, like annexation and road ownership, still need agreement, but confirmed the City\rquote s main goal is to adopt its own mobility fee so funds generated in Ocala are controlled by Ocala. The Council reiterated full support for moving to a city\u8209?controlled mobility\u8209?fee system and will revisit the matter once the next county meeting occurs.\par
\par
}

