\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Mr. Schatt encouraged the council to view Midtown as its own golf\u8209?cart\u8209?accessible district rather than waiting solely on a future crossing over SR 40. He noted that golf cart access boosts surrounding property values, as seen south of 40, and said similar access north of 40 would support Midtown\rquote s growth. He urged the city to establish a north\u8209?of\u8209?40 zone now and not rely entirely on FDOT\rquote s timeline.\par
\par
City Manager Pete Lee agreed the city can create a golf cart zone north of SR 40 independently and then work on connecting it across 40 later. He noted some residents already use street\u8209?legal carts to cross, and said staff will return with a phased plan, expanding the south area first and then adding north and west Ocala.\par
\par
}

