{\colortbl ;\red128\green128\blue128;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Internal Auditor Vincent Iovino summarized an investigation into an EFT fraud incident involving a compromised vendor email and improper verification of payment information. He explained that required safeguards were not followed, delays in escalation worsened the impact, and about $214,000 of the $292,000 lost was eventually recovered. The audit recommended periodic EFT\u8209?focused tabletop exercises to improve staff readiness, and management agreed to implement them in partnership with federal cybersecurity resources.\par
\par
Council Pro Tem Musleh commented on the amount of cybersecurity training City staff has, and questioned whether this incident would have happened if staff had followed procedures. Mr. Iovino agreed if staff had followed procedures, the fraud would not have been successful. \par
\par
}

