\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Police Chief Michael Balken presented the department\rquote s latest public safety report, noting 7,600 incidents, an 11 percent rise in reported crime, a 51 percent increase in arrests, and more than 1,200 traffic stops. He highlighted strong response times, averaging just over one minute for priority\u8209?one calls, and outlined current staffing, including only one vacancy and multiple recruits in training. Chief Balken credited the department\rquote s near\u8209?full staffing to competitive pay and the supportive culture created by city leadership and the community. Mayor Marciano praised the department\rquote s performance, emphasizing the positive culture, strong recruitment, and high standards that make Ocala an attractive place for law enforcement officers.\par
\par
}

