\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Strategic & Legislative Affairs Administrator Jeannine Robbins presented an overview of the City\rquote s 2026 employee engagement survey, explaining that the survey helps identify strengths and areas for improvement. The survey, administered in May, included 18 confidential questions across four areas: employees\rquote jobs, their immediate leaders, their teams, and their growth. Results showed a 93% overall satisfaction rate and an 88% willingness among employees to recommend the City as a great place to work, marking the third consecutive year with satisfaction above 91%. Over five years, satisfaction has remained consistently strong between 89% and 93%, with \ldblquote my job\rdblquote receiving the highest driver score and \ldblquote my growth\rdblquote the lowest, indicating a need for continued focus on training and development. Ms. Robbins also noted that only four of 60 comparable Florida municipalities conducted engagement surveys in 2026, placing Ocala among a small group leading this effort. She concluded by highlighting that these strong and consistent results are worth celebrating while still pointing to opportunities for continued improvement.\par
\par
}

