\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Chief Balken reported that overall public safety activity remained steady, with only a slight increase in total incidents. Officer\u8209?initiated calls rose by 2% while dispatched calls fell by 3%. Reported crimes increased 13%, though arrests remained the same at 217. Traffic enforcement rose significantly, with officers conducting 1,300 stops and handling 143 crashes. Violent crime showed a 22% increase, driven almost entirely by simple misdemeanor battery cases. Property and suicidal incident levels stayed flat. Priority\u8209?one response times improved sharply, averaging under one minute, while priority\u8209?two response times increased slightly. He noted recent high activity related to traffic crashes and stated that investigations are ongoing, with updates to follow.\par
