\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Growth Management Director Jeff Shrum presented the first of two required public hearings for an amendment to the existing development agreement for the KAS Ocala project, formerly known as the Ransom Group Investors Project. He explained that the amendment covers approximately 248 acres east of I\u8209?75 and south of SW 20th Street and incorporates the previously approved planned development plan, the associated traffic study, and a new section for tracking project trips. Mr. Shrum noted that the amendment consolidates the original 2004 agreement and subsequent amendments from 2008 and 2022. He stated that no action was required at this meeting and that the final public hearing is scheduled for November 3.\par
\par
The applicant, represented by Fred Roberts, stated that the amendment serves as a comprehensive cleanup of multiple past agreements and expressed readiness to answer questions or provide a presentation at the next meeting.\par
\par
}

