\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Mayor Marciano presented a proclamation to Beth McCall declaring November 14, 2026 as Look Up Marion, Put Down the Phone Day in the City of Ocala.\par
\par
Ms. McCall thanked City staff and committee members for their work on the initiative, noting it was launched in response to concerns from organizations serving children that identified technology use and its impact on youth as a top issue. She explained that the campaign promotes responsible technology use, not the elimination of technology, and highlighted that the QR code provides parents with resources through the Lookup Marion website. Ms. McCall encouraged families to participate in screen-free activities, engage with one another, and support efforts to address children's mental health.\par
\par
}

