\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Mr. Batsel, 1531 SE 36th Ave, explained that the requested representation is being reviewed under the City's established conflict-of-interest procedures, which were previously approved to ensure ethical compliance. He stated that, as former City Attorney, he cannot use any confidential information obtained during his representation of the City for the benefit of private clients. He noted that while he had limited involvement with matters related to the subject planned development, his law partner had extensive involvement, and under ethical rules any knowledge held by his partner is attributed to him. Mr. Batsel advised that the request involves representing a property owner seeking to rezone approximately 109 to 120 acres east of SW 49th Avenue by removing it from the Mockingbird PD and establishing a commercial node. After reviewing the matter and consulting with Mr. Gooding, he stated that neither he nor his firm possesses information from their prior representation of the City that would affect the proposed rezoning. He further stated that prospective clients are instructed to consult City counsel regarding potential conflicts before any representation proceeds.\par
\par
There being no further discussion the motion carried by roll call vote.\par
\par
}

