\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\f0\fs24 Chief Balken reported a 5% increase in overall police activity (7,530 incidents), driven by self-initiated officer activity, while dispatched calls decreased. Reported crimes decreased 12% to 286, arrests increased 6% to 209, and traffic enforcement activity increased 46%, with 1,270 traffic stops and an 8% increase in crashes. Crime trends remained generally consistent with the prior year, with a 34% decrease in quality-of-life crimes. Average response time remained strong at 1 minute, 10 seconds. Chief Balken also highlighted efforts to combat online child exploitation and promote the upcoming "Put Down Your Cell Phone Day" awareness campaign.\par
\par
}

